# Quill, on the Marrow's rail; then the pier at dawn.
dialogue quill4
  node farewell quill "Yellow flag on the boom, cargo. Quarantine: nobody off the Marrow sets foot in Port Vela. Except customs. Dorrit swears it's a regulation. Congratulations, you're a clerk again."
    -> farewell2
  node farewell2 quill "And if she's still at anchor when the dawn bell rings, Cray writes her down as a plague ship, and the harbour guns get to practise. So we sail at dawn. Either way."
    > "Then I have until dawn." -> until
      add aff 1
    > "I got a licence, a berth and a pirate captain in one night. Dawn's ages away." -> ages
    > "Come ashore. I'll write you a pass." -> pass
  node ages quill "That was the easy night, cargo. Nobody was trying to drown you on paper."
    -> until
  node pass quill "Signed by who? There's a lamp burning in Bramwick's window, and it isn't Bramwick. He's been up there since we dropped anchor. Writing."
    -> until
  node until quill "You have until dawn."
    -> beat
  node beat narrator "She looks at me a moment longer than the harbour needs."
    -> name
  node name quill "Fenn."
    -> noticed
  node noticed narrator "It's the first time she has ever said it. She sees me notice. I see her see me notice, and she glares at the lighthouse as if it started it."
    set farewell
    -> late
  node late quill "Don't be late."
    > "I'm never late. I'm a civil servant." -> civil
      add aff 1
    > "Say it again." -> again
      add aff 1
    > "(Nod, and go.)" -> END
  node civil quill "You're never early either. I've noticed. Go."
  node again quill "No. It's rationed. …Go on. The dawn isn't getting any later."
  # Talking up to the rail afterwards.
  node rail quill "Still here, cargo? The bell won't wait because you look worried. I've asked bells. They don't."
    > "We did it. Cray's finished." if inquiry_done -> done
    > "How's my father?" if not seen:quill4.dad -> dad
    > "How do I beat a man who writes everything down?" if not inquiry_done -> plan
    > "Show me the Liar again." if night_watch and not seen:quill4.liar -> liar
      add aff 1
    > "I'll be back before dawn." -> back
  node done quill "I heard. The whole harbour heard; Hobb cried on the capstan. Now get that flag off the boom, cargo. I want to stand on something that doesn't move."
  node dad quill "Up and down the rail. He's moved flag sixteen to our masthead so the town can see it. Vane let him. I've never seen Vane let anybody do anything."
    -> crates
  node crates quill "Vane found out what was in her crates. She's been very quiet. Hobb hid the cargo book, in case she wants to throw it at someone and picks him."
  node plan quill "You're asking the navigator? Good. He lies on paper, so take a bearing on every page he wrote and see where they cross. Start with Bramwick; he's where the lines meet."
  node liar quill "There. Low over the lighthouse. …It's moved since I showed you. It always moves. I like that about it. Go on. Go and be a clerk at somebody."
  node back quill "I know. I'm counting on it. I'm also counting the bells, so don't test me."
  # On the pier, once the quarantine's lifted and before the ledger's put right.
  node pier quill "Solid ground. I hate it. It just sits there. …The book, cargo. Fix the book, take it up the steps to Upper Town, then come and find me."
    > "You came ashore." -> ashore
    > "On my way." -> END
  node ashore quill "Vane said stretch my legs. I've stretched them as far as this bollard. It's a good bollard. I'm keeping it."
  # Dawn, on the pier: the choice.
  node dawn narrator "The sky over the headland has gone the colour of weak tea. Quill is on a bollard at the pier end, swinging one bare foot over the water, waiting for me as if she isn't."
    -> sea
  node sea quill "Well, cargo. Sea or desk? Your father's been home one night, and Bramwick needs somebody who reads the backs. I know what I'm asking."
    -> tide
  node tide quill "The tide doesn't care. I do. Don't tell the tide."
    > "You called me Fenn. Earlier." if not seen:quill4.once -> once
    > "Sign me on. Purser. I'll keep the books and you'll keep the stars." -> purser
    > "Someone has to keep the ledger honest. Come back every season?" -> season
    > "Upper Town first. I owe somebody up there an ending." if not seen:onn.home -> upfirst
  node once quill "Once. It's rationed. I'm saving the rest for when you've earned them."
    -> sea2
  node sea2 quill "So. Sea or desk? Take your time. Not that much."
    > "Sign me on. Purser. I'll keep the books and you'll keep the stars." -> purser
    > "Someone has to keep the ledger honest. Come back every season?" -> season
    > "Upper Town first. I owe somebody up there an ending." if not seen:onn.home -> upfirst
  node upfirst quill "Upper Town first, cargo. Go on. I was a lookout for years. Waiting's the job."
  node purser narrator "She tries very hard not to smile, and loses by a distance."
    -> biscuits
  node biscuits quill "Purser. Vane will make you count the biscuits."
    > "Then I'll count them beautifully." -> aboard
    > "(Kiss her.)" if aff >= 14 -> pkiss
  node pkiss narrator "I kiss her, on the pier, in front of the customs house, the lighthouse, and my father, who has found a reason to coil a rope very slowly nearby."
    -> logging
  node logging ansel "Don't mind me. I'm logging it."
    -> ptwo
  node ptwo quill "Get aboard, then. …Fenn. That's two. Don't get used to it."
    > "(Go aboard.)" -> END
      set ending_pirate
      act 4
  node aboard quill "Get aboard, then, cargo. The tide's turning. So, apparently, are you."
    > "(Go aboard.)" -> END
      set ending_pirate
      act 4
  node season narrator "She looks at the customs house for a long moment, and then back at me."
    -> every
  node every quill "Every season. I'll bring you a new star each time. You can write it down."
    > "I'll underline it." if night_watch -> quay
      add aff 1
    > "I'll stamp it." -> quay
    > "(Kiss her.)" if aff >= 14 -> dkiss
  node dkiss narrator "I kiss her. Behind us the customs-house window bangs open, Bramwick says “Regulation—”, Marta says “Shut that window, you old fool”, and he does. Slowly."
    -> dtwo
  node dtwo quill "Be on the quay when we come in, Fenn. That's two. I'll want a receipt."
    > "(Watch her go.)" -> END
      set ending_desk
      act 4
  node quay quill "Be on the quay when we come in. Don't be late."
    > "(Watch her go.)" -> END
      set ending_desk
      act 4
